WEBVTT

1
00:00:35.421 --> 00:00:37.442
(BIRDS SQUAWKING)

2
00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:47.956
- (ALARM BEEPS)
- (MAN GROANS)

3
00:01:52.825 --> 00:01:54.860
(DOGS BARKING)

4
00:01:57.548 --> 00:02:00.871
MAN: Good morning, guys.
How's it going? Bailey, what's up?

5
00:02:00.951 --> 00:02:05.208
What's up? Hey, Chewy.
Hey, Watson, how's it going?

6
00:02:05.288 --> 00:02:08.052
Looking good. Queenie, Rascal.

7
00:02:09.776 --> 00:02:13.297
Okay. Want some food, want some food?

8
00:02:13.797 --> 00:02:16.673
Wolf it down.
That's it, that's all you get.

9
00:02:16.753 --> 00:02:18.422
Water?

10
00:02:19.222 --> 00:02:20.722
(WATER SPRINKLING)

11
00:02:28.161 --> 00:02:30.150
- (WHINES)
- How are you?

12
00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.953
There she is, there she is.

13
00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:36.257
Okay, all right, Lexi, all right. Hey.

14
00:02:36.837 --> 00:02:40.771
Back it up, back it up.
Hey, Lexi. Back it up.

15
00:02:41.241 --> 00:02:45.296
Hey, hey. Hey, big doggie.
Big doggie, big doggie.

16
00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:53.802
(MUFFLED MUSIC PLAYING)

17
00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.555
(STOP REQUEST CHIMES)

18
00:03:20.781 --> 00:03:22.770
Holly, right?

19
00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.272
Holly Garling.

20
00:03:25.352 --> 00:03:28.175
Hi. How are you?

21
00:03:28.255 --> 00:03:30.677
Hi. I'm sorry, do we know each other?

22
00:03:30.757 --> 00:03:33.480
Oh, Seth. West Brook High.

23
00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.767
- Oh. Were you in my class?
- Oh, I was in the year above you.

24
00:03:36.847 --> 00:03:40.671
We didn't hang out or anything,
but I knew who you were.

25
00:03:40.751 --> 00:03:44.245
- You did?
- Sure, everybody did.

26
00:03:45.305 --> 00:03:47.494
I don't know about that.

27
00:03:48.074 --> 00:03:51.464
So you're a writer now, huh?
That's cool. That's great.

28
00:03:51.544 --> 00:03:56.770
Yeah. This whole waitressing uniform,
it's just a disguise.

29
00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.039
It's convincing.

30
00:03:59.119 --> 00:04:01.685
I was gonna order an ice cream sundae.

31
00:04:02.455 --> 00:04:05.623
- Extra sprinkles.
- You wouldn't be the first.

32
00:04:12.165 --> 00:04:14.459
- This is my stop.
- Oh, this is you?

33
00:04:17.353 --> 00:04:18.942
It was nice to see you again.

34
00:04:19.022 --> 00:04:21.895
Nice to see you too.
Hey, if you're not doing anything...

35
00:04:21.975 --> 00:04:23.801
get a coffee.

36
00:04:37.357 --> 00:04:39.430
(MUFFLED MUSIC PLAYING)

37
00:04:59.579 --> 00:05:01.212
Hmm.

38
00:05:10.355 --> 00:05:12.190
- (TV INDISTINCT)
- SETH: Hey.

39
00:05:16.996 --> 00:05:19.080
There he is. There's the man.

40
00:05:26.172 --> 00:05:29.029
- Nate, let me ask you a question.
- Hmm?

41
00:05:29.109 --> 00:05:32.465
If there was this girl
and you wanted her to notice you...

42
00:05:32.545 --> 00:05:34.855
Are you serious right now?

43
00:05:35.282 --> 00:05:36.703
Yeah.

44
00:05:36.783 --> 00:05:39.557
Shit, man, I don't know you.
I don't know what kind of game you got.

45
00:05:39.637 --> 00:05:43.510
- What are you asking me?
- Sorry. I thought maybe...

46
00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.807
Listen, wait...

47
00:05:45.887 --> 00:05:49.074
you like this girl?
We are talking about a girl here, right?

48
00:05:49.154 --> 00:05:51.651
Yes, girl. I do like her.

49
00:05:51.731 --> 00:05:54.020
So just confident, you know?

50
00:05:54.114 --> 00:05:56.687
Guy who's confident.
Knows how to make them laugh.

51
00:05:56.767 --> 00:05:59.182
Tell 'em about your day.
Act like you give a shit.

52
00:05:59.262 --> 00:06:01.228
I mean, it ain't a mystery.

53
00:06:01.308 --> 00:06:05.365
Confident, funny, make 'em laugh.
Got it. Good. Thanks.

54
00:06:05.445 --> 00:06:07.968
Hey, and no more bringing
this shit to me, all right?

55
00:06:08.048 --> 00:06:11.271
You and me, we ain't like that.

56
00:06:11.351 --> 00:06:13.092
- Cool.
- (TAPS)

57
00:06:18.291 --> 00:06:20.313
Seth, Dr. Jessup needs your help.

58
00:06:20.393 --> 00:06:23.049
He's putting down
the German Shepherd in 34.

59
00:06:23.129 --> 00:06:25.085
- Lexi.
- Look, you're a sweet guy.

60
00:06:25.165 --> 00:06:29.529
But if you can't do your job,
I'll find someone who can. Is that clear?

61
00:06:29.609 --> 00:06:31.745
She's a really good dog.

62
00:06:33.673 --> 00:06:36.296
Hey, Lexi. Hey.

63
00:06:36.376 --> 00:06:39.814
Here's the thing, we just... Hey, girl.

64
00:06:45.385 --> 00:06:48.541
Hey, Lexi. Hey.

65
00:06:48.621 --> 00:06:51.264
How's it going? Wanna go for a walk?

66
00:06:51.624 --> 00:06:53.246
Hey, hey, hey.

67
00:06:53.326 --> 00:06:55.816
Good girl. Yeah, it's exciting, isn't it?

68
00:06:56.196 --> 00:06:58.272
All right, Lexi. Here we go.

69
00:07:00.667 --> 00:07:04.591
All right, that's a good dog.
Yeah, that's a good dog.

70
00:07:04.671 --> 00:07:07.327
- DR. JESSUP: You all right?
- Yeah, she's just a good dog.

71
00:07:07.407 --> 00:07:10.547
- It's okay, Lexi. It's all right.
- You want her, you can always keep her.

72
00:07:10.627 --> 00:07:14.801
- My building doesn't allow pets. Very strict.
- Fucking find a new place.

73
00:07:14.881 --> 00:07:17.938
$9.00 an hour?
I'm lucky I have running water.

74
00:07:18.018 --> 00:07:20.173
That's your whole problem.
You got no initiative.

75
00:07:20.253 --> 00:07:22.943
It's how come you're still working
in a shit hole like this at your age.

76
00:07:23.023 --> 00:07:26.213
You want something in this life,
you gotta take it. (SIGHS)

77
00:07:27.243 --> 00:07:30.354
So what's it gonna be?
I mean, you want her, she's yours.

78
00:07:33.767 --> 00:07:35.523
Do it, do it already.

79
00:07:36.736 --> 00:07:40.243
All right, Lexi. Here we go.
You're a good dog.

80
00:07:40.323 --> 00:07:42.757
Hold still. You're a good dog.

81
00:08:13.273 --> 00:08:15.363
(FAINT SCRAPING)

82
00:08:49.626 --> 00:08:51.684
(FAINT MUSIC PLAYING)

83
00:09:59.912 --> 00:10:03.803
SETH: Hey, Holly, hey.
What time do you get lunch?

84
00:10:03.883 --> 00:10:07.874
What time do you get lunch?
I get lunch at 1:00.

85
00:10:07.954 --> 00:10:10.043
1:00.

86
00:10:10.723 --> 00:10:13.759
Hey, hey, hi. Hey.

87
00:10:13.839 --> 00:10:16.383
Hey, remember me?

88
00:10:16.963 --> 00:10:19.184
That's right. Uh...

89
00:10:19.264 --> 00:10:22.555
Well, I guess table for one
while I'm here,

90
00:10:22.635 --> 00:10:28.628
but really I was just wondering
if you wanted to get maybe dinner later.

91
00:10:28.708 --> 00:10:32.732
I... I don't know about you,
but I love seafood.

92
00:10:32.812 --> 00:10:36.169
Oh, you do? Yeah, that's all I eat.

93
00:10:36.249 --> 00:10:39.806
Seafood, seafood... There's a, uh...
there's a place on...

94
00:10:39.886 --> 00:10:45.078
There's a place on... there's a place
on Wilshire called the Crab Joint.

95
00:10:45.158 --> 00:10:49.327
Oh, you know it?
Yeah, we could... tonight?

96
00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:54.220
It's... hey, Holly, hey.

97
00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:57.236
Hey, Holly. How's it going? Hey.

98
00:11:14.521 --> 00:11:17.377
- Hi. Anywhere?
- Yeah, anywhere is fine.

99
00:11:17.457 --> 00:11:19.990
Okay. Thanks.

100
00:11:34.173 --> 00:11:37.330
Hey, how are you? I'm Holly.
I'll be taking care of you today.

101
00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:40.003
- You must be a writer.
- I'm sorry?

102
00:11:40.083 --> 00:11:45.115
A writer. The disguise from the bus.

103
00:11:46.019 --> 00:11:49.096
We met a couple of days ago on the bus.
My name's Seth.

104
00:11:49.176 --> 00:11:51.844
I'm so sorry.
My memory, it like totally sucks.

105
00:11:51.924 --> 00:11:54.213
I know, just what you want
to hear from your waiter, right?

106
00:11:54.293 --> 00:11:55.548
No, that's fine.

107
00:11:55.628 --> 00:11:58.418
Can I get you started with anything?
An appetizer?

108
00:11:58.498 --> 00:12:00.453
Yeah, um...

109
00:12:00.533 --> 00:12:04.190
Let's uh... let's do water.

110
00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:07.694
And then by the time
you come back, I'll know.

111
00:12:07.774 --> 00:12:10.263
Water. <i>Una agua</i>. You got it.

112
00:12:10.343 --> 00:12:12.932
Hey, um, I like your hair.

113
00:12:13.012 --> 00:12:15.001
It looks different from the bus.

114
00:12:15.081 --> 00:12:16.703
- It's nice.
- Thank you.

115
00:12:16.783 --> 00:12:22.509
Yeah. You shouldn't feel insecure
about it or self conscious, it's...

116
00:12:22.789 --> 00:12:25.101
is a good haircut.

117
00:12:26.848 --> 00:12:30.450
Why don't you take a look at the menu
and I will go grab your water.

118
00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:32.852
Yeah. Pie.

119
00:12:32.932 --> 00:12:35.133
Apple pie.

120
00:12:58.057 --> 00:12:59.712
How's it going over here?

121
00:12:59.792 --> 00:13:02.616
- Seth.
- What's that?

122
00:13:03.196 --> 00:13:05.652
Seth. My name is Seth.

123
00:13:05.932 --> 00:13:07.820
How's the food, Seth?

124
00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:10.223
It's good. It's quality.

125
00:13:10.303 --> 00:13:13.193
Actually, I had a question for you.

126
00:13:13.273 --> 00:13:14.861
Do you like Ben Folds?

127
00:13:14.941 --> 00:13:17.630
'Cause I have a couple of tickets
to his concert this week

128
00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:20.100
and the girl I was gonna go with,
not a girlfriend or anything,

129
00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:22.635
she can't make it, she has a thing.

130
00:13:22.715 --> 00:13:26.139
I was wondering if maybe you'd wanna...

131
00:13:26.219 --> 00:13:27.907
- go?
- I'm sorry, I can't.

132
00:13:27.987 --> 00:13:31.744
I don't like going to shows by myself,
it feels kind of strange, so maybe...

133
00:13:31.824 --> 00:13:33.246
Not a big deal, no pressure.

134
00:13:33.326 --> 00:13:36.115
We could just go. It wouldn't
have to be a date or anything.

135
00:13:36.195 --> 00:13:39.385
The thing is, I already
sort of have a boyfriend, so...

136
00:13:39.465 --> 00:13:41.507
No, you don't.

137
00:13:45.438 --> 00:13:47.827
I'm just gonna leave this here.
Thanks for coming in.

138
00:13:47.907 --> 00:13:50.341
Hang on a second.

139
00:14:38.725 --> 00:14:40.257
(BRANCH SNAPS)

140
00:14:54.757 --> 00:14:56.781
(PEOPLE ON TV CHATTERING)

141
00:14:58.411 --> 00:15:01.667
MAN ON TV: <i>But, like, when they do speak,
you know you're in trouble.</i>

142
00:15:01.747 --> 00:15:02.980
Hey.

143
00:15:04.984 --> 00:15:08.808
- There's a guy out there.
- Ooh, is he hot?

144
00:15:08.888 --> 00:15:10.610
I'm serious, Claire.

145
00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:14.425
Don't get paranoid on me, Hol.
You're no fun when you're paranoid.

146
00:15:15.561 --> 00:15:17.450
- Never mind.
- (CELL PHONE RINGS)

147
00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:20.048
Ten bucks says it's him.

148
00:15:23.035 --> 00:15:25.191
- Yes, Eric.
- ERIC: <i>Hey, babe.</i>

149
00:15:25.271 --> 00:15:28.127
- HOLLY: What do you want?
- ERIC: <i>Jesus, what's with the attitude?</i>

150
00:15:28.207 --> 00:15:30.730
<i>I just wanted to talk.
I've been thinking about you.</i>

151
00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:33.666
- Is he drunk and weepy again?
- A little bit.

152
00:15:33.746 --> 00:15:35.768
Eric:
<i>Who are you talking to? You with someone?</i>

153
00:15:35.848 --> 00:15:40.540
Don't get paranoid on me, Eric.
You're no fun when you're paranoid.

154
00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.541
(SNICKERS)

155
00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:51.351
CLAIRE: So the other night with Eric?

156
00:15:51.831 --> 00:15:54.554
Really? Are we gonna go there again?

157
00:15:54.634 --> 00:15:58.224
He was two years, you can't
convince me he never mattered.

158
00:15:58.404 --> 00:16:02.940
I'm serious, though, Hol.
Being alone is just kinda shitty.

159
00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:07.099
So, what, I'm just supposed
to forget everything he did?

160
00:16:07.179 --> 00:16:10.903
Yes. Forget, forgive.
Move the fuck on already.

161
00:16:10.983 --> 00:16:13.417
Just go back to the way things were.

162
00:16:15.955 --> 00:16:18.363
You know I can't do that.

163
00:16:27.033 --> 00:16:29.166
To us.

164
00:16:33.906 --> 00:16:35.929
Hey, Sam.

165
00:16:36.809 --> 00:16:38.868
- Someone's popular.
- What?

166
00:16:38.948 --> 00:16:41.295
We put it in the break room.

167
00:16:42.615 --> 00:16:44.061
Okay.

168
00:17:03.536 --> 00:17:08.372
Lucky, bitch. Spill. Who's the guy?

169
00:17:20.086 --> 00:17:23.110
- Hey.
- Hey.

170
00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:27.747
Listen, I'm so sorry for the drunk dial the
other night. I mean, you know how it is.

171
00:17:27.827 --> 00:17:29.382
Yeah, I do.

172
00:17:29.462 --> 00:17:32.635
Listen, can I get you a beer or something?

173
00:17:32.715 --> 00:17:37.023
Eric, you have to stop
doing stuff like this.

174
00:17:37.103 --> 00:17:40.460
Stuff like... what now?

175
00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:44.014
Come on. Roses?
You know they're my favorite.

176
00:17:44.844 --> 00:17:47.187
I didn't know that.

177
00:17:48.714 --> 00:17:51.954
Okay. Well, now I just feel stupid.

178
00:17:52.184 --> 00:17:54.818
- Well... just one beer.
- I should go.

179
00:17:56.255 --> 00:17:59.913
It wasn't all bad, right?
We had some good times.

180
00:18:00.893 --> 00:18:02.515
Yep.

181
00:18:02.895 --> 00:18:05.324
So why don't we give it another shot?

182
00:18:06.566 --> 00:18:09.153
Are you really gonna make me say her name?

183
00:18:18.744 --> 00:18:21.301
ERIC: This is so fucking stupid.

184
00:18:21.381 --> 00:18:24.337
- I mean, we had something.
- Had.

185
00:18:25.017 --> 00:18:27.285
Eric, past tense.

186
00:18:31.523 --> 00:18:33.622
I'm gonna get some air.

187
00:18:56.799 --> 00:18:58.679
SETH: Nice night.

188
00:19:00.052 --> 00:19:02.586
- Yeah.
- Yep.

189
00:19:04.624 --> 00:19:08.181
- Not a smoker?
- Me? No.

190
00:19:09.261 --> 00:19:12.585
(EXHALES) That's good.
Don't ever start, it's a terrible habit.

191
00:19:12.665 --> 00:19:16.057
Okay, I won't. Thanks.

192
00:19:30.282 --> 00:19:33.484
- Have a nice night.
- You like the flowers?

193
00:19:34.687 --> 00:19:38.745
You seemed like a red and white roses
kind of girl. It was just a guess.

194
00:19:38.825 --> 00:19:40.917
Oh, my God.
You're that guy from the restaurant.

195
00:19:40.997 --> 00:19:42.632
Seth.

196
00:19:43.566 --> 00:19:47.220
- Are you, like, following me or something?
- What? No. Just...

197
00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:51.026
Look, I'm not some psycho, okay?
You know me.

198
00:19:51.106 --> 00:19:53.860
- We went to school together.
- What do you want?

199
00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:57.099
I don't want anything.
I just want to talk to you.

200
00:19:57.179 --> 00:20:02.218
When I saw you on the bus the other day,
after all these years, I felt something.

201
00:20:02.298 --> 00:20:05.638
I know you did.
I can't just walk away from that.

202
00:20:05.718 --> 00:20:08.942
- I don't even know you.
- But you will.

203
00:20:09.622 --> 00:20:14.013
- You can go, I just... can I just talk to you?
- No. Don't! Don't touch me.

204
00:20:14.093 --> 00:20:16.215
- Move!
- Are you kidding me?

205
00:20:16.295 --> 00:20:18.784
- SETH: Just let me talk to you.
- Fuck you. Fuck you!

206
00:20:18.864 --> 00:20:20.946
- Just let me explain.
- He tried to grab me.

207
00:20:21.026 --> 00:20:23.623
SETH: What? No.
Hey, that is not true at all, man.

208
00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:26.536
Fuck off.

209
00:20:27.239 --> 00:20:28.628
(WHIMPERS)

210
00:20:28.708 --> 00:20:32.030
- Did he hurt you?
- I'm fine. I'm fine.

211
00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:35.101
- (CHUCKLES)
- You think this is funny?

212
00:20:35.181 --> 00:20:38.905
- Eric, stop. Stop it. Stop it.
- Laugh it up, dick head.

213
00:20:39.985 --> 00:20:42.686
Let me handle this. Hey. Come on.

214
00:20:44.089 --> 00:20:46.512
Get the fuck away from her.

215
00:20:46.592 --> 00:20:48.881
Don't you ever come back here.

216
00:20:49.161 --> 00:20:50.987
(GROANS)

217
00:20:51.067 --> 00:20:53.114
(COUGHS)

218
00:22:14.046 --> 00:22:17.903
- Maybe if you retrace your steps.
- No. It's gotta be here somewhere.

219
00:22:17.983 --> 00:22:21.418
Well, was your name in it?
Or like any contact information?

220
00:22:23.756 --> 00:22:25.888
What do you think?

221
00:22:40.940 --> 00:22:43.024
(SEAGULLS SQUAWKING)

222
00:24:00.686 --> 00:24:02.719
(CLATTERS)

223
00:24:09.395 --> 00:24:11.334
(TAPS)

224
00:24:57.343 --> 00:24:59.377
(CLANGS)

225
00:25:22.801 --> 00:25:24.835
(CLANGS)

226
00:28:38.163 --> 00:28:40.618
- (SCREAMS)
- (SPRAYS)

227
00:28:43.835 --> 00:28:46.102
(COUGHING) You fucking bitch!

228
00:28:50.275 --> 00:28:52.318
(COUGHS)

229
00:29:14.166 --> 00:29:16.684
- (HOMELESS MAN YELLS)
- (GLASS SHATTERS)

230
00:30:40.819 --> 00:30:42.325
(FAINT CLATTERING)

231
00:30:48.460 --> 00:30:51.294
Claire? You here?

232
00:31:47.953 --> 00:31:49.975
(MUFFLED SCREAMING)

233
00:31:50.405 --> 00:31:51.777
Shh.

234
00:31:51.857 --> 00:31:55.180
What I just put in you
is called pancuronium bromide.

235
00:31:55.260 --> 00:31:58.384
It's a paralyzing agent.
It stings a little.

236
00:31:59.064 --> 00:32:02.599
Don't worry, it's safe.
I tested it on myself.

237
00:32:11.776 --> 00:32:13.762
(FAINT MUSIC PLAYING)

238
00:32:15.380 --> 00:32:17.391
