493
00:55:00.878 --> 00:55:03.514
So that was all an act?

494
00:55:06.450 --> 00:55:08.906
You were just humoring him?

495
00:55:08.986 --> 00:55:12.255
- Playing along...
- If you've got something to say...

496
00:55:12.723 --> 00:55:16.059
I'm just making sure
your head's still in the game.

497
00:55:17.961 --> 00:55:21.118
I don't need another
useless pep talk, Claire.

498
00:55:21.198 --> 00:55:23.313
And I don't need you.

499
00:55:48.725 --> 00:55:50.267
Yes?

500
00:55:51.896 --> 00:55:54.964
What? No. Nothing.

501
00:55:55.566 --> 00:55:58.422
Just was curious.

502
00:55:58.602 --> 00:56:00.387
Why you did it.

503
00:56:01.372 --> 00:56:04.628
I guess, when I saw Eric's email,
all those messages from Claire...

504
00:56:04.708 --> 00:56:07.331
No, not Claire. I understand that.

505
00:56:07.411 --> 00:56:10.101
It's a crime of passion or whatever.

506
00:56:10.981 --> 00:56:13.437
I wanna know why you didn't stop there.

507
00:56:13.517 --> 00:56:15.806
Why you killed the others.

508
00:56:15.886 --> 00:56:19.610
'Cause you feel guilty for what you did
to Claire, for getting away with it.

509
00:56:19.690 --> 00:56:21.812
You wanted to get caught, didn't you?

510
00:56:21.892 --> 00:56:25.128
No, because I could.

511
00:56:26.196 --> 00:56:28.652
Yeah, I don't believe that.

512
00:56:28.732 --> 00:56:30.855
Well, I don't care what you believe.

513
00:56:31.235 --> 00:56:32.957
'Cause see, here's the thing, Seth.

514
00:56:33.037 --> 00:56:35.892
When someone dies in front of you,
the way Claire died,

515
00:56:35.972 --> 00:56:39.076
it's like you're whole world
just snaps into focus.

516
00:56:40.444 --> 00:56:43.000
- Cry for help?
- It was a way to pass the time.

517
00:56:43.080 --> 00:56:45.169
Don't pretend you know what I am.

518
00:56:45.249 --> 00:56:48.606
You're wrong, I do know you.
I know you from this.

519
00:56:48.686 --> 00:56:51.509
And the girl who wrote this,
you had dreams.

520
00:56:51.589 --> 00:56:55.445
She cared about people.
Who's scared to be alone.

521
00:56:55.525 --> 00:56:59.066
This is the real you. Not...

522
00:57:05.636 --> 00:57:08.055
Seth's got a little crush.

523
00:57:09.740 --> 00:57:11.462
This isn't about us.

524
00:57:11.542 --> 00:57:14.164
If you love something, set it free.

525
00:57:14.244 --> 00:57:16.179
Isn't that how that goes?

526
00:57:18.215 --> 00:57:20.450
You know I can't do that.

527
00:57:22.019 --> 00:57:24.274
Do you know what happens
to a great white shark

528
00:57:24.354 --> 00:57:26.978
when you put him inside an aquarium?

529
00:57:27.958 --> 00:57:30.714
It bashes its brains against the glass.

530
00:57:30.794 --> 00:57:32.716
Every time.

531
00:57:32.796 --> 00:57:34.430
- Come on.
- (SMACKS)

532
00:57:34.510 --> 00:57:38.659
Stop, Holly, stop! Stop, Holly!

533
00:57:40.204 --> 00:57:44.884
What are you gonna do when you come down here
tomorrow and I'm belly up in the tank, huh?

534
00:57:45.309 --> 00:57:47.211
'Cause you can't just walk away.

535
00:57:47.411 --> 00:57:50.378
Not with your fingerprints
all over the place.

536
00:57:51.668 --> 00:57:55.999
I kill myself, your life ends too.

537
00:58:00.758 --> 00:58:05.679
So how's that for the boundaries
of our fucking relationship?

538
00:58:14.855 --> 00:58:16.925
(DOOR OPENS, CLOSES)

539
00:58:22.079 --> 00:58:24.139
(DOGS BARKING)

540
00:58:34.024 --> 00:58:36.094
(HUMMING)

541
00:58:46.636 --> 00:58:47.725
- Seth?
- Hmm?

542
00:58:47.805 --> 00:58:50.540
Finish this up
and come see me in my office.

543
00:58:56.713 --> 00:58:58.302
Something wrong?

544
00:58:58.382 --> 00:59:01.067
"Is something wrong?"
That's the question, isn't it?

545
00:59:02.986 --> 00:59:05.042
I'm not following you.

546
00:59:05.122 --> 00:59:08.205
The kennels are filthy.
We've got bugs up in the stock room.

547
00:59:08.285 --> 00:59:11.381
And where's Seth?
He's not here, that's for sure.

548
00:59:11.461 --> 00:59:13.383
Nate says you haven't
been here in two days.

549
00:59:13.463 --> 00:59:16.006
Mrs. Gundy, Nate is hardly...

550
00:59:16.089 --> 00:59:18.255
Nate does his job.

551
00:59:18.335 --> 00:59:20.625
You should've done yours.

552
00:59:21.705 --> 00:59:24.995
- You're firing me?
- Disciplinary notice.

553
00:59:25.375 --> 00:59:29.232
This goes in your permanent record.
One more strike and you're gone. Understand?

554
00:59:29.312 --> 00:59:32.815
Understood. Thank you.
You don't know how much this means to me.

555
00:59:38.655 --> 00:59:42.546
<i>This, this is what's gonna happen to you
when you think you're in control.</i>

556
00:59:42.626 --> 00:59:45.049
<i>You think you're in control, Holly.</i>

557
00:59:45.829 --> 00:59:49.987
<i>Well, this is what'll happen
when you think you're in...</i>

558
00:59:50.067 --> 00:59:51.952
<i>I control the situation.</i> (ECHOING)

559
00:59:58.842 --> 01:00:01.565
There's the man.
Just doing some maintenance.

560
01:00:01.645 --> 01:00:03.713
Didn't ask.

561
01:00:08.051 --> 01:00:10.520
Hey, Seth. I got your paycheck.

562
01:00:25.135 --> 01:00:27.404
Still here, huh?

563
01:00:33.175 --> 01:00:34.976
Where's the rest?

564
01:00:37.313 --> 01:00:39.065
There is no rest.

565
01:00:39.145 --> 01:00:41.872
This is what happens when you start
acting like you're in control.

566
01:00:41.952 --> 01:00:45.789
- That's not enough.
- You don't get to decide that.

567
01:00:45.869 --> 01:00:47.711
Fuck you.

568
01:00:47.791 --> 01:00:52.182
Fuck me? I go through hell for you
and what do you do, threaten me?

569
01:00:52.262 --> 01:00:56.102
You ever pull that shit again, I'll show you
what a real hunger strike feels like.

570
01:00:56.182 --> 01:00:58.018
Fuck you.

571
01:01:05.275 --> 01:01:08.110
I had a dream last night
and you were in it.

572
01:01:09.979 --> 01:01:13.704
It was just the two of us, and we were
in this house down by the water.

573
01:01:14.784 --> 01:01:17.941
I think we'd been living there a long time
'cause there were these pictures on the walls.

574
01:01:18.021 --> 01:01:19.855
Pictures of us.

575
01:01:21.191 --> 01:01:24.145
It was weird looking at them, because...

576
01:01:24.725 --> 01:01:26.983
something about it felt right.

577
01:01:27.064 --> 01:01:30.377
Like this, this whole world
is a dream and...

578
01:01:30.757 --> 01:01:33.770
that house on the beach, that's reality.

579
01:01:34.938 --> 01:01:37.507
That's how things are supposed to be.

580
01:01:45.949 --> 01:01:49.173
SETH: Maybe I can get you some snacks
from the vending machine.

581
01:01:49.553 --> 01:01:51.408
Thanks, Seth.

582
01:01:51.488 --> 01:01:53.005
(DOOR CLOSES)

583
01:03:19.408 --> 01:03:21.231
Holy shit.

584
01:03:21.511 --> 01:03:23.199
There's a light on the wall.

585
01:03:28.685 --> 01:03:30.540
Hey, what's your name?

586
01:03:30.620 --> 01:03:33.076
Um, I'm Nate.

587
01:03:33.156 --> 01:03:34.844
Listen to me, Nate.

588
01:03:34.924 --> 01:03:38.615
You have to find something to break
open this lock. Can you do that?

589
01:03:38.695 --> 01:03:41.185
What kind of fucked up...

590
01:03:42.065 --> 01:03:44.767
- Did Seth do this?
- Nate, there's no time for that right now.

591
01:04:06.890 --> 01:04:10.580
- Okay, go at it hard, at an angle.
- We gotta call somebody, the cops.

592
01:04:10.660 --> 01:04:13.162
You have to get me out of here right now.

593
01:04:19.337 --> 01:04:21.372
(NATE AND HOLLY FAINTLY MURMURING)

594
01:04:30.613 --> 01:04:34.704
- NATE: That's what I'm doing.
- HOLLY: No, just... Harder.

595
01:04:34.784 --> 01:04:37.263
NATE: This is all fucked up.

596
01:04:38.955 --> 01:04:42.479
- Okay, that's great.
- NATE: Okay, on three. All right?

597
01:04:42.559 --> 01:04:45.365
One, two, three.

598
01:04:45.445 --> 01:04:47.517
(STRAINING)

599
01:04:50.797 --> 01:04:53.556
- (PANTING) Hold on.
- Do you know what real love is, Nate?

600
01:04:53.636 --> 01:04:55.373
What?

601
01:04:55.453 --> 01:05:00.063
HOLLY: You know, real love.
Say you loved somebody. But she got sick.

602
01:05:00.143 --> 01:05:03.300
And then someone came along
one day to pull the plug on her

603
01:05:03.380 --> 01:05:06.873
to take her away from you forever.
What would you do?

604
01:05:07.674 --> 01:05:10.041
- I just wanna get you outta here.
- You would do anything

605
01:05:10.121 --> 01:05:12.108
to stop that from happening.

606
01:05:12.188 --> 01:05:17.493
Anything at all, no matter what the cost
because that's... what love is.

607
01:05:19.462 --> 01:05:21.731
Love is sacrifice.

608
01:05:24.200 --> 01:05:26.224
(SMACKS)

609
01:05:26.604 --> 01:05:28.678
NATE: What the fuck?

610
01:05:29.272 --> 01:05:31.561
You die.

611
01:05:31.941 --> 01:05:35.199
Oh. Are you stabbing me?

612
01:05:36.279 --> 01:05:38.234
(SCREAMS)

613
01:05:39.649 --> 01:05:41.651
Motherfucker!

614
01:05:46.122 --> 01:05:49.979
The block, Seth. Use the cinder block.
He's moving. Come on, use it.

615
01:05:50.059 --> 01:05:52.182
- I can't.
- You have to.

616
01:05:52.262 --> 01:05:54.217
Seth, I can't lose you.

617
01:05:54.397 --> 01:05:56.653
- Please?
- NATE: Oh, fuck.

618
01:05:56.733 --> 01:05:58.735
(NATE SCREAMS)

619
01:06:00.470 --> 01:06:02.739
I can feel my leg. (SCREAMS)

620
01:06:04.874 --> 01:06:06.943
What the fuck?

621
01:06:10.580 --> 01:06:12.862
Somebody help me.

622
01:06:12.942 --> 01:06:14.506
(GROANS)

623
01:06:16.886 --> 01:06:18.689
- Oh, my...
- (CRASHES)

624
01:06:20.757 --> 01:06:23.192
Come on, do it again.

625
01:06:31.801 --> 01:06:33.953
One more time.

626
01:06:37.907 --> 01:06:39.762
I'm sorry, I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

627
01:06:39.842 --> 01:06:42.866
Seth. You have to listen to me, okay?

628
01:06:42.946 --> 01:06:46.569
You have to do exactly what I say.
Are you listening?

629
01:06:46.649 --> 01:06:50.524
Okay, step one is disposing of the body.
The sooner, the better.

630
01:06:50.604 --> 01:06:54.244
Okay, burn it, bury it, sink it, whatever.
Just get it out of here.

631
01:06:54.324 --> 01:06:57.217
<i>But you can't do that
before you get rid of the identifiers.</i>

632
01:06:57.297 --> 01:07:00.006
<i>Teeth, tattoos, fingerprints.</i>

633
01:07:00.086 --> 01:07:02.719
<i>The fingerprints are easy,
you can use a carob for that.</i>

634
01:07:02.819 --> 01:07:06.556
<i>After the teeth, you need to scatter them.
Dumpsters, in water, whatever.</i>

635
01:07:06.636 --> 01:07:09.246
<i>Just not all in the same place.</i>

636
01:07:09.326 --> 01:07:12.040
And then there's
just the body to worry about.

637
01:07:14.744 --> 01:07:19.081
- SETH: <i>He's not gonna fit in the incinerator.</i>
- HOLLY: <i>Well, not like that.</i>

638
01:08:05.228 --> 01:08:07.230
(FIRE ERUPTS)

639
01:08:24.247 --> 01:08:27.082
HOLLY: <i>Do you want to practice
with me what to say?</i>

640
01:08:30.620 --> 01:08:33.255
SETH: <i>Hey, Mrs. Gundy, it's Seth.</i>

641
01:08:34.824 --> 01:08:39.416
Sorry to call you so late. Um, yeah,
Nate asked me to watch the front

642
01:08:39.496 --> 01:08:42.085
while he ran some errands
and he's still not back yet.

643
01:08:42.165 --> 01:08:44.454
I don't know where he went.

644
01:08:44.734 --> 01:08:47.357
Oh... Okay, good night.

645
01:08:47.637 --> 01:08:49.272
Sorry.

646
01:09:37.120 --> 01:09:38.975
How do you feel?

647
01:09:39.055 --> 01:09:41.545
I don't know. Disconnected.

648
01:09:41.825 --> 01:09:43.580
Like it happened
to someone else, you know?

649
01:09:43.660 --> 01:09:46.316
The first time's always the worst.

650
01:09:46.696 --> 01:09:50.083
There is no first time.
It was an accident. I told you.

651
01:09:50.163 --> 01:09:52.489
You know what always got to me?

652
01:09:52.969 --> 01:09:54.904
It was the questions.

653
01:09:54.984 --> 01:09:58.991
I remember in the beginning all I could
think about was what if she had a pet?

654
01:09:59.576 --> 01:10:02.374
It's poor little doggie just...

655
01:10:02.454 --> 01:10:05.799
sitting by the door
waiting for her to come home.

656
01:10:06.049 --> 01:10:08.305
But all that goes away.

657
01:10:08.685 --> 01:10:12.842
The more you think about it, the more
you remember the parts that you liked.

658
01:10:12.922 --> 01:10:14.611
How it made you feel.

659
01:10:14.691 --> 01:10:17.331
Like you were in control of your life
for the very first time,

660
01:10:17.411 --> 01:10:20.149
- like nothing could hurt you.
- That's not how it was.

661
01:10:20.229 --> 01:10:22.785
But the only problem is...

662
01:10:22.865 --> 01:10:25.934
that sooner or later
it all goes back to normal.

663
01:10:26.970 --> 01:10:31.294
All of a sudden you're nothing special,
you're just you.

664
01:10:31.374 --> 01:10:33.129
Stop, okay?

665
01:10:33.209 --> 01:10:35.591
And that's when you start to wonder.

666
01:10:35.671 --> 01:10:38.801
How far you'd have to go
to get that feeling back.

667
01:10:38.881 --> 01:10:40.236
It's not the same.

668
01:10:40.316 --> 01:10:44.707
There is no shame
in accepting what you are, Seth.

669
01:10:44.787 --> 01:10:47.103
I did it to keep us safe. I had no choice.

670
01:10:47.183 --> 01:10:49.446
Didn't you ever wonder why...

671
01:10:50.226 --> 01:10:53.983
all the girls in the world
but you get a hard on for me?

672
01:10:54.063 --> 01:10:56.732
And you think that's, what, a coincidence?

673
01:10:57.834 --> 01:11:00.857
You and me, we were born to do this.

674
01:11:01.337 --> 01:11:03.500
Don't act like you know
a goddamn thing about me.

675
01:11:03.580 --> 01:11:06.496
I know that a normal person
finds a murder confession

676
01:11:06.576 --> 01:11:08.932
and goes to the police, not to PetSmart.

677
01:11:09.012 --> 01:11:12.665
Oh, yeah, "Excuse me, Officer.
You see that girl over there, the waitress?

678
01:11:12.745 --> 01:11:16.139
She's Hannibal Lecter. You know how I know?
I broke into her apartment and stole her shit."

679
01:11:16.219 --> 01:11:19.228
- That'll work?
- Oh, and so plan B is kidnapping?

680
01:11:19.308 --> 01:11:23.416
'Cause the fucking alternative was sitting
around watching you hurt someone else.

681
01:11:23.496 --> 01:11:25.232
Mm.

682
01:11:26.162 --> 01:11:28.652
Good thing no one got hurt.

683
01:11:29.132 --> 01:11:32.555
I told you... I told you.

684
01:11:32.835 --> 01:11:35.859
- It's an accident.
- Face it, Seth.

685
01:11:36.439 --> 01:11:40.096
This was never about
saving lives, you like this.

686
01:11:40.476 --> 01:11:42.965
You like having that kind of power.

687
01:11:43.245 --> 01:11:45.335
Deciding who lives, who dies.

688
01:11:45.415 --> 01:11:47.167
Holly...

689
01:11:47.485 --> 01:11:52.055
it's not too late. I can save you, please.

690
01:11:53.790 --> 01:11:56.626
Please. I can save you.

691
01:12:00.163 --> 01:12:02.317
Maybe you're not supposed to save me.

692
01:12:06.035 --> 01:12:08.738
Maybe I'm suppose to save you.

693
01:12:12.375 --> 01:12:14.510
Don't, don't.

694
01:12:31.494 --> 01:12:35.618
Oh, Seth, please help me, I'm so cold.
Please make me warm.

695
01:12:35.698 --> 01:12:38.888
Can you help me,
can you please make me warm?

696
01:12:38.968 --> 01:12:40.369
(MOANS)

697
01:12:44.773 --> 01:12:47.529
I thought you loved me.

698
01:12:49.679 --> 01:12:51.513
I do.

699
01:12:54.150 --> 01:12:56.217
I do love you.

700
01:12:57.554 --> 01:13:01.223
Holly. Holly.

701
01:13:05.495 --> 01:13:07.130
Holly.

702
01:13:12.602 --> 01:13:14.770
I'll come back as soon as I can.

703
01:13:27.550 --> 01:13:30.073
- Oh.
- Seth.

704
01:13:30.153 --> 01:13:32.174
This is Detective Mira.

705
01:13:32.754 --> 01:13:36.459
- Something wrong?
- DETECTIVE: Is there somewhere we can talk?

706
01:13:37.827 --> 01:13:40.049
So, you work with Nathan, yeah?

707
01:13:40.129 --> 01:13:41.751
Yes.

708
01:13:42.031 --> 01:13:44.621
When's the last time you saw him?

709
01:13:44.701 --> 01:13:46.723
Wednesday, I think? Wednesday evening.

710
01:13:46.803 --> 01:13:49.492
Yeah, he asked me to cover
the front while he ran some errands.

711
01:13:49.572 --> 01:13:52.596
- What kind of errands?
- Um, he didn't say.

712
01:13:53.476 --> 01:13:56.132
Uh-huh. And this would be about...

713
01:13:56.212 --> 01:13:58.067
what time?

714
01:13:58.247 --> 01:14:00.332
9:00, 10:00. Something like that.

715
01:14:01.751 --> 01:14:04.307
- He leave out through the front?
- Yeah.

716
01:14:04.587 --> 01:14:06.743
The front door, you sure?

717
01:14:06.823 --> 01:14:08.911
Yeah, why?

718
01:14:08.991 --> 01:14:13.817
Well, here's the thing. The front door
operates on a keyless entry system.

719
01:14:14.297 --> 01:14:17.687
As you know, it records
each instance in or out.

720
01:14:18.267 --> 01:14:21.692
Now you wanna guess
the last time someone opened that door?

721
01:14:22.772 --> 01:14:25.966
- 4:00. That's 4:00 a.m.
- Huh.

722
01:14:26.046 --> 01:14:29.465
And you said it was what, 9:00 or 10:00 p.m.?
It's kind of weird, don't you think?

723
01:14:29.545 --> 01:14:31.367
No, maybe I'm remembering it wrong.

724
01:14:31.447 --> 01:14:35.071
He could have left out the side door,
or loading docks.

725
01:14:35.151 --> 01:14:39.108
Loading docks? Oh, shit. Yeah.

726
01:14:39.188 --> 01:14:41.289
I should check that out.

727
01:14:42.992 --> 01:14:44.881
You and Nathan friends?

728
01:14:44.961 --> 01:14:47.013
Well, we worked together.
He was a nice guy and all.

729
01:14:47.093 --> 01:14:50.653
- Until he tried to get you fired.
- What? Oh. That is not what happened.

730
01:14:50.733 --> 01:14:53.690
- Nate and I were friends.
- Oh, now you're friends again.

731
01:14:53.770 --> 01:14:56.492
Or you were friends, past tense.

732
01:14:56.572 --> 01:14:58.795
That's the second time you said that.

733
01:14:58.875 --> 01:15:03.296
Well, you know what they say. First time's
confusion, second time's confession.

734
01:15:03.913 --> 01:15:06.736
- What's this about?
- Standard procedure.

735
01:15:06.816 --> 01:15:09.105
So now, he asked you to cover for him,

736
01:15:09.185 --> 01:15:13.209
this is what Wednesday night, nine or ten?
Did he say where he was going?

737
01:15:13.289 --> 01:15:16.345
I think he had to meet someone.
He got a phone call, something.

738
01:15:16.425 --> 01:15:19.490
It's funny,
because the first thing we did...

739
01:15:20.216 --> 01:15:21.807
was check the phone records.

740
01:15:21.887 --> 01:15:25.425
And the last person
he talked to was his girlfriend.

741
01:15:25.505 --> 01:15:27.720
5:32 that afternoon.

742
01:16:28.798 --> 01:16:30.499
SETH: Hi.

743
01:16:35.805 --> 01:16:37.874
Gotta eat something.

744
01:16:42.645 --> 01:16:45.582
Holly, come on.

745
01:16:49.018 --> 01:16:52.754
Come on. Come on, don't do this.

746
01:17:20.449 --> 01:17:22.673
SETH: Now I know what you're doing.

747
01:17:23.753 --> 01:17:25.988
It's not gonna work.

748
01:17:28.491 --> 01:17:31.660
Just talk to me, please.

749
01:17:37.967 --> 01:17:39.969
HOLLY: It's over, Seth.

750
01:17:42.204 --> 01:17:44.274
I don't understand.

751
01:17:46.242 --> 01:17:48.497
Because if you can't help me...

752
01:17:49.077 --> 01:17:52.714
if you can't give me what I need,
then no one can.

753
01:17:54.283 --> 01:17:57.987
Tell me, tell me what you need.

754
01:18:00.456 --> 01:18:02.679
You know the answer.

755
01:18:03.159 --> 01:18:05.449
You put me in a box.

756
01:18:06.829 --> 01:18:09.631
That's not love, that's ownership.

757
01:18:13.802 --> 01:18:16.171
You didn't give me anything.

758
01:18:18.507 --> 01:18:21.097
All you did was take.

759
01:18:21.677 --> 01:18:23.726
I can't let you out.

760
01:18:24.046 --> 01:18:27.404
- You know that.
- I didn't ask you to.

761
01:18:27.934 --> 01:18:29.988
Then what? What do you want?

762
01:18:35.858 --> 01:18:37.279
Proof.

763
01:18:39.728 --> 01:18:41.456
Proof?

764
01:18:43.165 --> 01:18:46.222
- A finger.
- A what?

765
01:18:46.702 --> 01:18:48.503
A finger?

766
01:18:50.973 --> 01:18:52.544
My finger?

767
01:18:59.548 --> 01:19:00.970
No.

768
01:19:01.050 --> 01:19:04.841
No. No. No. No.

769
01:19:05.061 --> 01:19:07.076
This is fucked.

770
01:19:07.156 --> 01:19:09.178
Can't you see that?

771
01:19:09.258 --> 01:19:11.548
This is totally fucked.

772
01:19:12.828 --> 01:19:15.985
No. I'm trying to save you here.

773
01:19:16.165 --> 01:19:17.720
And I'm trying to let you.

774
01:19:17.800 --> 01:19:22.024
Well, you can't ask me for that, Holly.
And I'm not gonna do it.

775
01:19:25.841 --> 01:19:28.377
I used to think I was the only one.

776
01:19:30.679 --> 01:19:33.170
Even when I was a kid, I still knew.

777
01:19:34.350 --> 01:19:38.356
That if they ever found out,
my family, my friends...

778
01:19:39.788 --> 01:19:43.424
If they knew what I really was,
they'd run the other way.

779
01:19:47.429 --> 01:19:49.798
And so you learn to...

780
01:19:52.068 --> 01:19:54.604
blend in, to fake it.

781
01:19:57.773 --> 01:19:59.930
After a while...

782
01:20:01.010 --> 01:20:04.405
you don't even notice
how lonely you really are.

783
01:20:10.169 --> 01:20:12.204
But then...

784
01:20:14.790 --> 01:20:17.417
someone comes along,

785
01:20:17.497 --> 01:20:19.660
someone like you.

786
01:20:22.631 --> 01:20:25.603
Even if he just doesn't know it yet.

787
01:20:27.536 --> 01:20:31.690
And all of a sudden, you start thinking...

788
01:20:33.542 --> 01:20:35.751
maybe it doesn't have to be this way.

789
01:20:38.046 --> 01:20:40.379
Maybe I don't have to be alone.

790
01:20:41.616 --> 01:20:44.353
And so let go of the rope.

791
01:20:47.256 --> 01:20:50.386
Because this person,
he's not gonna let you fall.

792
01:20:50.466 --> 01:20:53.061
He's gonna catch you. You know it.

793
01:20:58.334 --> 01:21:01.370
At least that's what you
keep telling yourself.

794
01:21:03.739 --> 01:21:06.208
The whole way down.

795
01:21:24.927 --> 01:21:26.995
Don't come back.

796
01:21:28.330 --> 01:21:31.203
If that's all I am to you,
if I'm just a pet.

797
01:21:33.802 --> 01:21:35.510
Then don't come back for me.

798
01:21:36.972 --> 01:21:39.174
Don't come back for me.

799
01:21:54.290 --> 01:21:56.294
(DOGS WHINING)

800
01:24:12.027 --> 01:24:14.851
If I do this for you...

801
01:24:15.931 --> 01:24:18.053
then you'll believe?

802
01:24:18.133 --> 01:24:19.638
Yes.

803
01:24:33.515 --> 01:24:35.371
This is wrong.

804
01:24:35.451 --> 01:24:39.808
Seth, you love me.
There is nothing more right than that.

805
01:24:47.729 --> 01:24:49.731
(GROANS)

806
01:24:53.669 --> 01:24:55.157
(WHIMPERS)

807
01:24:55.237 --> 01:24:56.838
You're almost there.

808
01:24:59.942 --> 01:25:02.030
(SCREAMS)

809
01:25:02.110 --> 01:25:04.647
- (CRUNCHES)
- (SCREAMING CONTINUES)

810
01:25:08.784 --> 01:25:10.704
Open the door.

811
01:25:12.488 --> 01:25:14.910
- What are you doing?
- Open the fucking door.

812
01:25:14.990 --> 01:25:18.793
You're already down a finger, Seth.
How much more are you ready to lose?

813
01:25:29.271 --> 01:25:31.307
(GROANS)

814
01:25:35.427 --> 01:25:37.295
Get back.

815
01:26:04.506 --> 01:26:06.141
Holly.

816
01:26:08.310 --> 01:26:10.699
Wait. What are you doing?

817
01:26:10.779 --> 01:26:12.481
Shh.

818
01:26:21.990 --> 01:26:24.059
I believe you.

819
01:26:29.298 --> 01:26:31.166
You do?

820
01:26:34.269 --> 01:26:36.105
Do you...

821
01:26:41.844 --> 01:26:44.079
You saved me, Seth.

822
01:26:45.614 --> 01:26:48.083
Of course I love you.

823
01:27:02.598 --> 01:27:05.000
But you know what that means.

824
01:27:07.703 --> 01:27:09.685
(CHOKING, GARGLING)

825
01:27:15.777 --> 01:27:17.533
(SETH GASPS) Holly.

826
01:27:18.013 --> 01:27:20.049
Don't leave me.

827
01:27:34.096 --> 01:27:36.152
(PANTING)

828
01:27:37.532 --> 01:27:39.421
Oh, God.

829
01:27:39.501 --> 01:27:41.537
(MOANS)

830
01:28:01.890 --> 01:28:03.846
ERIC: You've been working
on these pieces for years.

831
01:28:03.926 --> 01:28:06.114
Holly:
I know, I'm not saying I'm not excited.

832
01:28:06.294 --> 01:28:08.357
It's like great to get that call.
I just...

833
01:28:08.437 --> 01:28:12.321
I figured you'd be more psyched about this.
It's a big deal, getting published.

834
01:28:12.401 --> 01:28:15.190
It's just a vanity press,
it's not exactly "The New Yorker."

835
01:28:15.270 --> 01:28:17.393
Screw that, it's still awesome.

836
01:28:17.673 --> 01:28:21.063
- I'm proud of you.
- I thought you didn't even like my story.

837
01:28:21.143 --> 01:28:22.677
I like you.

838
01:28:25.213 --> 01:28:26.468
(PHONE BUZZES)

839
01:28:26.548 --> 01:28:28.891
- Hey, babe, can you grab my phone?
- Yeah.

840
01:28:30.352 --> 01:28:32.506
(MAN CHATTERING ON TV)

841
01:29:09.491 --> 01:29:11.379
Here you go.

842
01:29:11.459 --> 01:29:13.460
Thank you, babe.

843
01:29:51.967 --> 01:29:53.602
Hi.

844
01:29:58.106 --> 01:30:00.562
(SIGHS) I had another bad day with Eric.

845
01:30:00.642 --> 01:30:03.665
He's still fooling around
with other girls.

846
01:30:03.945 --> 01:30:07.148
This morning I almost hurt him.

847
01:30:09.851 --> 01:30:12.020
But then I thought of you.

848
01:30:19.361 --> 01:30:21.763
And how much you love me.

849
01:30:24.533 --> 01:30:26.835
And what you're doing for me.

850
01:30:29.905 --> 01:30:31.973
Then I felt better.

851
01:30:46.855 --> 01:30:48.859
(MUSIC PLAYING)

852
01:32:49.711 --> 01:32:51.715
(MUSIC CHANGES)

853
01:33:50.305 --> 01:33:52.106
(MUSIC ENDS)
